+        # Full-trust delegation ("一次做完" / " autonome 托管"). The user hands the whole task over
+        # and stops reading messages: every decision the agent would normally escalate is made by
+        # the model itself, and a blocking question that goes unanswered for `autonomy_wait_seconds`
+        # is answered by picking the most reasonable branch and continuing — never by failing
+        # closed. Reversibility is what makes this safe: `checkpoints.enabled` must be true so any
+        # branch the user rejects can be restored instantly via /rollback.
+        #   mode: "off" (default; prompt for decisions) | "auto" (self-decide only after the
+        #         autonomy_wait_seconds timeout) | "always" (self-decide from the first decision).
+        #   autonomy_wait_seconds: how long a blocking clarify may sit unanswered before the agent
+        #         picks a branch itself. Only consulted in "auto" mode; 0 = no waiting.
+        #   irreversible_ok: when false (strongly recommended), genuinely irreversible actions
+        #         (force-push, rm -rf of source data, dropping a database, purchasing) still
+        #         escalate to the human even in "always" mode. Turn it on only with a live
+        #         checkpoint and a rollback path you trust.
+        "autonomy": {
+            "mode": "off",
+            "autonomy_wait_seconds": 300,
+            "irreversible_ok": False,
+        },
         # System-prompt guidance telling the model to call tools instead of describing actions.
